<title>SPAIN: Spanish Treasury sets new issues at lower coupon.</title>
<headline>Spanish Treasury sets new issues at lower coupon.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Spanish Treasury announced on Friday it will issue the following bonds  KSPM and  KSPY on July 1 and 2:</p>
<p>Bono 31/1/01  5.00 pct</p>
<p>Bono 31/1/03  5.25 pct</p>
<p>Bono 31/1/08  6.00 pct</p>
<p>Bono 31/1/13  6.15 pct</p>
<p>All coupons are lower than the ones of the previous issues.</p>
<p>These are the first issues of strippable debt. Legal entities will not have to pay the 25 percent withholding tax on new strippable debt.</p>
<p>In a separate statement, the Spanish government said that strips will be possible when new issuance will reach a minimum outstanding volume of one trillion pesetas.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
